# CODEOWNERS — review routing for Solidus FinOps
#
# Each line maps a path pattern to one or more owners. Owners are
# automatically requested as reviewers when a PR touches matching files.
# Last-match wins; the catch-all at the top is overridden by the more
# specific rules below.
#
# Replace @ivankovtun with your team's GitHub handles before adopting.
# For a team owner, use the @org/team-name form (requires the team to
# exist in the org).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default reviewer for any file in the repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root composition + cross-cutting contract
#
# Changes here affect every consumer. Require maintainer review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/main.tf                                @ivankovtun
/variables.tf                           @ivankovtun
/outputs.tf                             @ivankovtun
/locals.tf                              @ivankovtun
/providers.tf                           @ivankovtun
/versions.tf                            @ivankovtun
/CHANGELOG.md                           @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation
#
# Adjust the docs-owner team if you have a dedicated docs reviewer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/README.md                              @ivankovtun
/CONTRIBUTING.md                        @ivankovtun
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md                     @ivankovtun
/SECURITY.md                            @ivankovtun
/SUPPORT.md                             @ivankovtun
/docs/                                  @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-module ownership
#
# Map each module to the team that operates the AWS service it manages.
# A platform-team / SRE team is a reasonable default; route specific
# modules to specialised teams as needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/modules/alerting/                      @ivankovtun
/modules/budgets/                       @ivankovtun
/modules/cost-data-exports/             @ivankovtun
/modules/finops-metrics/                @ivankovtun
/modules/idle-resource-cleanup/         @ivankovtun
/modules/instance-scheduler/            @ivankovtun
/modules/tag-governance/                @ivankovtun

# Lambda Python sources — code review by anyone in the maintainer set
**/lambda/**/*.py                       @ivankovtun
**/scripts/*.sh                         @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security-sensitive paths — require additional review
#
# Use a separate `@<org>/security` team if you have one. Two-reviewer
# branch protection rules + CODEOWNERS together give you a four-eyes
# control on these paths.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                                @ivankovtun
/NOTICE                                 @ivankovtun
/SECURITY.md                            @ivankovtun
**/iam.tf                               @ivankovtun
**/kms*.tf                              @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI + governance configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                               @ivankovtun
/.tflint.hcl                            @ivankovtun
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                @ivankovtun
/.editorconfig                          @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Examples — anyone can suggest improvements, maintainer signs off
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/examples/                              @ivankovtun

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagrams — visual changes should be reviewed by someone who can render them
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/diagrams/                              @ivankovtun
